[{:db/id "q-317304/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5a288b65-8b71-5aea-9ff8-fdf518da6529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317304/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b17956e5-6ff6-5f04-9344-be6df426cdb0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317304/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-317304/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317304" :question/id #uuid "f8084faa-c83e-5fad-abf5-bedd210fd50c" :question/math-academy-id "q-317304" :question/problem "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨0,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨7,\\,-2,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨0,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩\\cdot ⟨7,\\,-2,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩ \\\\  & =(0)(7)+(5)(-2)+(\\sqrt{11})(\\sqrt{11}) \\\\  & =0-10+11 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317304/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ba6b6b5-ac1d-5a3a-876a-af51fdf50e0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317304"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73458/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" :answer/id #uuid "d09e15a4-7c13-568e-a570-fc9e3902259d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73458/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "a92c2ee1-6a99-5609-b4e3-631380d9c995" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73458/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "9e82e3a2-053e-5768-8a34-8f3d881ac045" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73458/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "94c25a54-1110-5d27-b12b-bbc3dcb2c220" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73458/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" :answer/id #uuid "4e729854-4bf1-5961-beb3-ba1a72b2c6d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73458/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5058bb6e-7250-5d26-8ec4-d5b0a463e069" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73458/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3" :answer-field/choices ["q-73458/selection/283bc09f1a097ae8400558511ca45f1013e17c797fdb7407be52694190fd744b" "q-73458/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" "q-73458/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" "q-73458/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-73458/selection/23c0b4da815e7ba954fedc5e75955047cfe471feec4d2029849a63511c000fa3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73458" :question/id #uuid "6d564fbe-e6b5-5480-8918-6d6776762bbd" :question/math-academy-id "q-73458" :question/problem "Given that $a=⟨-2,4,3⟩,$ $b=⟨-1,3,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,-1,4⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 4-2\\cdot (-1))i-((-1)\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 2)j+((-1)\\cdot (-1)-3\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =14i+8j-5k \\\\  & =⟨14,8,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-2,4,3⟩\\cdot ⟨14,8,-5⟩ \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot 14+4\\cdot 8+3\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73458/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ba6b6b5-ac1d-5a3a-876a-af51fdf50e0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73458"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73459/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "eb8877e6-767d-58e7-b176-1f5f6c2f2e72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73459/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "afab3324-438b-5276-b49e-7969bc2eb9f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73459/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "a9cfe596-e861-5273-a5e2-95fd4d21ab3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73459/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "48465873-5c8f-504f-a6d0-ce053462ea2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73459/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "72a718ff-6323-558a-a858-67fc7e2271a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73459/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8aee5a4-6f62-54f7-bdf9-b5eefaadfa02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73459/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-73459/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-73459/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-73459/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-73459/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-73459/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73459" :question/id #uuid "753f723d-a0a1-5e8a-8afb-5f9d1f35cfae" :question/math-academy-id "q-73459" :question/problem "Given that $a=⟨-2,0,-1⟩,$ $b=⟨-2,-1,0⟩,$ and $c=⟨3,1,4⟩,$ find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using the definition of the scalar triple product." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\times c & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 1)i-((-2)\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3)j+((-2)\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =-4i+8j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the scalar triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-2,0,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,8,1⟩ \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73459/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ba6b6b5-ac1d-5a3a-876a-af51fdf50e0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73459"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-20063"] :question/problem "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨1,0,2⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨-2,1,8⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨1,0,2⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,8⟩ \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)+0\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-317302/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "f04a743f-843d-5a0f-b8c0-a4589a3b9158" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-317302/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "365eded9-c6b0-5308-b4dd-28f04dbd12ce" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-317302/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-317302/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-317302" :question/id #uuid "1e96fc98-4911-5113-ab88-6925162a0a47" :question/math-academy-id "q-317302" :question/problem "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{7})+(-2)(3)+(5)(-1) \\\\  & =7-6-5 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-317302/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ba6b6b5-ac1d-5a3a-876a-af51fdf50e0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317302"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-20050/selection/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "788fa611-640d-59dd-b2fb-ea5d01bc150c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-